        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>Table of Contents</title>\n  <script>\n    window.MathJax = {\n      tex: { inlineMath: [['$', '$']], displayMath: [['$$', '$$']] },\n      svg: { fontCache: 'global' }\n    };\n  </script>\n  <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-svg.js\" async></script>\n  <style>\n    html, body {\n      margin: 0;\n      min-height: 100%;\n      background: #fff;\n      color: #000;\n      font-family: \"Times New Roman\", Times, serif;\n    }\n    .page {\n      width: 1700px;\n      min-height: 2200px;\n      box-sizing: border-box;\n      padding: 49px 50px 0;\n      position: relative;\n    }\n    .toc {\n      margin: 0;\n      color: #0000b8;\n      font-size: 27px;\n      line-height: 1;\n      font-weight: normal;\n    }\n    .heading {\n      margin: 71px 0 0;\n      font-size: 28px;\n      line-height: 1.15;\n      font-weight: normal;\n    }\n    p {\n      margin: 37px 0 0;\n      font-size: 28px;\n      line-height: 1.13;\n      font-weight: normal;\n    }\n    .indent {\n      text-indent: 55px;\n    }\n    .second {\n      margin-top: 37px;\n    }\n    .peer-tables {\n      width: 1282px;\n      margin: 41px auto 0;\n      display: flex;\n      align-items: flex-start;\n      gap: 14px;\n    }\n    table {\n      border-collapse: collapse;\n      table-layout: fixed;\n      font-size: 28px;\n      line-height: 1.08;\n    }\n    .left-table {\n      width: 570px;\n    }\n    .right-table {\n      width: 570px;\n    }\n    th {\n      height: 25px;\n      padding: 0;\n      border-bottom: 2px solid #000;\n      font-size: 20px;\n      line-height: 1;\n      font-weight: bold;\n      text-align: center;\n      vertical-align: bottom;\n    }\n    th.name {\n      text-align: center;\n    }\n    td {\n      padding: 0;\n      height: 30px;\n      vertical-align: top;\n      white-space: nowrap;\n    }\n    td.company {\n      padding-right: 7px;\n      text-align: left;\n    }\n    td.mark {\n      text-align: center;\n    }\n    .right-table td.company {\n      padding-left: 0;\n    }\n    .page-number {\n      margin-top: 41px;\n      text-align: center;\n      font-size: 27px;\n      line-height: 1;\n    }\n    .footer-line {\n      position: absolute;\n      left: 50px;\n      right: 47px;\n      top: 1701px;\n      height: 6px;\n      background: #808080;\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div class=\"page\">\n    <div class=\"toc\">Table of Contents</div>\n\n    <div class=\"heading\">Committee's own judgment of the results achieved by our CEO as compared to goals established at the beginning of the fiscal year.</div>\n\n    <p class=\"indent\">As mentioned above, the Compensation Committee reviews relevant market and industry practices on compensation packages to monitor<br>the market practices for compensating our desired talent pool, including data from our Peer Companies (as described below) for the three major<br>components of our compensation program. The Compensation Committee, however, does not set compensation components to meet specific<br>benchmarks, such as targeting salaries \"at the 50 <sup>th</sup> percentile\" or equity compensation \"at the 75 <sup>th</sup> percentile\". Rather, the Compensation<br>Committee reviewed this peer data as a reference point in determining whether each executive's compensation level properly reflects the<br>executive's role and scope of responsibilities relative to our peers and companies with whom we compete for talent.</p>\n\n    <p class=\"indent second\">For fiscal year 2010, our human resources department obtained the full Radford Executive Survey of 149 companies, or the Radford<br>Companies. From the list of Radford Companies, Hewitt and our human resources department recommended and our Compensation Committee<br>approved, with only minor changes from the recommendations, three different groups of Peer Companies: employee peers, executive peers and<br>semiconductor peers. Employee peers are the companies in various industries with which we feel we generally compete for talent. Executive<br>peers are a subset of the employee peer list that (i) had revenue levels of $500 million to $5 billion, and thus were similar in size to our<br>anticipated revenue levels for fiscal year 2010, and (ii) had an established business and market presence and, thus, were similar in complexity.<br>Semiconductor peers are all the companies in the semiconductor industry from the Radford Executive Survey. For fiscal year 2010, our<br>employee peers (listed under the column titled \"EE\" below), executive peers (listed under the column titled \"EX\" below) and semiconductor<br>peers (listed under the column titled \"SC\" below) consisted of the companies listed below, or our Peer Companies.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"peer-tables\">\n      <table class=\"left-table\">\n        <colgroup>\n          <col style=\"width:438px\">\n          <col style=\"width:44px\">\n          <col style=\"width:44px\">\n          <col style=\"width:44px\">\n        </colgroup>\n        <thead>\n          <tr><th class=\"name\">Company Name</th><th>EE</th><th>EX</th><th>SC</th></tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td class=\"company\">Adobe Systems, Inc.</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td><td class=\"mark\"></td></tr>\n          <tr><td class=\"company\">Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td></tr>\n          <tr><td class=\"company\">Agilent Technologies, Inc.</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td><td class=\"mark\"></td></tr>\n          <tr><td class=\"company\">Altera Corporation</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td></tr>\n          <tr><td class=\"company\">Amazon.Com, Inc.</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td><td class=\"mark\"></td></tr>\n          <tr><td class=\"company\">Apple Inc.</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td><td class=\"mark\"></td></tr>\n          <tr><td class=\"company\">Autodesk, Inc.</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td><td class=\"mark\"></td></tr>\n          <tr><td class=\"company\">Avago Technologies Limited</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td><td class=\"mark\"></td><td class=\"mark\"></td></tr>\n          <tr><td class=\"company\">Broadcom Corporation</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td></tr>\n          <tr><td class=\"company\">Cadence Design Systems, Inc.</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td><td class=\"mark\"></td><td class=\"mark\"></td></tr>\n          <tr><td class=\"company\">Cisco Systems, Inc.</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td><td class=\"mark\"></td><td class=\"mark\"></td></tr>\n          <tr><td class=\"company\" style=\"padding-top:30px\">Cypress Semiconductor Corporation</td><td class=\"mark\" style=\"padding-top:30px\">X</td><td class=\"mark\" style=\"padding-top:30px\">X</td><td class=\"mark\" style=\"padding-top:30px\">X</td></tr>\n          <tr><td class=\"company\">Dell Inc.</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td><td class=\"mark\"></td><td class=\"mark\"></td></tr>\n          <tr><td class=\"company\" style=\"padding-top:30px\">Ebay Inc.</td><td class=\"mark\" style=\"padding-top:30px\">X</td><td class=\"mark\" style=\"padding-top:30px\">X</td><td class=\"mark\" style=\"padding-top:30px\"></td></tr>\n          <tr><td class=\"company\" style=\"padding-top:30px\">Electronic Arts Inc.</td><td class=\"mark\" style=\"padding-top:30px\">X</td><td class=\"mark\" style=\"padding-top:30px\">X</td><td class=\"mark\" style=\"padding-top:30px\"></td></tr>\n          <tr><td class=\"company\">EMC Corporation</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td><td class=\"mark\"></td><td class=\"mark\"></td></tr>\n          <tr><td class=\"company\">Ericsson Inc.</td><td class=\"mark\">X</td><td class